Ivan,
If you are using rtracklayer::import, you will produce a RangedData 
object and you can extract the RangesList component using the ranges() 
function.

library(rtracklayer)
myRegions <- import('myregions.bed')
myRangesList <- ranges(myRegions)



Patrick


